e_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MjQzNTc3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44243577?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Max191","html_url":"https://github.com/Max191","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Max191/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Max191/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Max191/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Max191/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Max191/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Max191/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Max191/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Max191/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Max191/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### What happened?\n\nWe are seeing non-deterministic results in Llama 405b when exporting 4 or more attention layers. It seems like there is an issue loading the weights properly since the left hand side of the `torch.aten.mm` is constant over multiple runs, but the right hand side - which is derived from the `output.weight` weight tensor - cannot be saved to numpy via `iree-run-module`. The output of the `torch.aten.mm` is always non-deterministic, so it leads me to believe the issue has to do with loading the weight tensors. I have a small repro [here](https://gist.github.com/aviator19941/eadef1c8d4c2748f6edc8107fa6f4cda) with repro instructions below.\n\n### Steps to reproduce your issue\n\n1. Login to the `smci355-ccs-aus-n10-09` machine which uses rocm 7.0.\n2. Download repro.mlir: \n```\nwget https://gist.githubusercontent.com/aviator19941/eadef1c8d4c2748f6edc8107fa6f4cda/raw/d90b978bfd60f8d1271f60f344a87c63efaf7892/repro.mlir\n```\n3. Download compile, run, and compare scripts and input:\n```\nwget https://gist.githubusercontent.com/aviator19941/c72ade6f44d6f10c0efaec7740f8bbf4/raw/2e25e4cea36a13148e2f5e7ed3a626d3865eaf37/compile.sh\nwget https://gist.githubusercontent.com/aviator19941/7420935f6868353eae3f5ad00af68234/raw/e04b42caccbd602f4d37eec5dccc5fe6f1e948c0/run_repro.sh\nwget https://gist.githubusercontent.com/aviator19941/4d0c7b5a8964f3d7a0e74cf9d93cddff/raw/74a503a03e0b5657dd1d1fd18b9623546ed36cdc/compare_results.py\nwget https://sharkpublic.blob.core.windows.net/sharkpublic/halo-models/llm-dev/llama3_405b/repro_input.npy\n```\n4. Set up venv:\n```\npython3.11 -m venv .test\nsource .test/bin/activate\npip install -f https://iree.dev/pip-release-links.html --upgrade --pre \\\n  iree-base-compiler iree-base-runtime\n```\n5. Run scripts:\n```\n./compile.sh && ./run_repro.sh && python compare_results.py\n```\n\n\n### What component(s) does this issue relate to?\n\n_No response_\n\n### Version information\n\niree-base-compiler 3.7.0rc20250725\niree-base-runtime  3.7.0rc20250725\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_","closed_by":{"login":"MaheshRavishankar","id":1663364,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NjMzNjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1663364?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaheshRavishankar","html_url":"https://github.com/MaheshRavishankar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaheshRavishankar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaheshRavishankar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaheshRavishankar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaheshRavishankar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaheshRavishankar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaheshRavishankar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.gi